 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Keeping the quantity word",
     "texto": [
      "Unlike English, where we usually drop it and just say «I have three», in Italian **ne** must be kept next to the number or quantifier: **Quante mele compri? Ne compro due** (How many apples are you buying? I'm buying two)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Common quantifiers",
     "texto": [
      "**un po'** (a bit), **alcuni/alcune** (some), **molti/molte** (many), **nessuno** (none), **abbastanza** (enough): **Vuoi del formaggio? Sì, ne prendo un po'**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Question",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Answer with «ne»",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Translation",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
